1
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,190
Two weeks. I said I could do it in two weeks, and I did it.

2
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:21,430
The pictures you've taken are fabulous, Richard.

3
00:02:21,430 --> 00:02:23,240
Mr. Carlson will love them.

4
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:25,130
Monday morning.

5
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:27,270
I'm going to show him the photos on Monday morning.

6
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:31,110
I can't wait!

7
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:37,140
I'm very proud of you. You really did a beautiful job.

8
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:41,840
I know he will love the new photographs for your book.

9
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:46,820
Yeah. I really did do a good job, didn't I?

10
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:50,560
Hey, you know? There's still some film left on this roll,

11
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:53,060
and there's one person I haven't photographed in a long time.

12
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:53,820
Who?

13
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,760
You.

14
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:59,170
Richard! I haven't brushed my hair. Richard,

15
00:02:59,170 --> 00:02:59,790
You look great!

16
00:02:59,790 --> 00:03:07,040
It's not fair, Richard. I'm not even ready.

17
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:34,380
Oh, that's wonderful! That's wonderful!

18
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:37,810
Thanks.

19
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:38,590
Fabulous!

20
00:03:38,590 --> 00:03:41,060
Thanks.

21
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:43,120
Terrific!

22
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,560
Thanks.

23
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:47,060
They get better and better.

24
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,470
Thanks a lot.

25
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:51,840
This is sensational!

26
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:55,390
Yeah. Thanks.

27
00:03:55,390 --> 00:03:58,900
What a job! Good work, Richard!

28
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,330
I'm so glad you like them so much.

29
00:04:01,330 --> 00:04:05,180
Like them? They represent your best work.

30
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:06,090
Really?

31
00:04:06,090 --> 00:04:08,190
Absolutely.

32
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:14,450
Well ... what do you think? Do I have my book?

33
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:22,100
You do. You do. There's a book here.

34
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,470
I'll have a contract

35
00:04:23,470 --> 00:04:24,730
and an advance payment waiting for you

36
00:04:24,730 --> 00:04:25,810
first thing in the morning.

37
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:27,970
Thank you.

38
00:04:27,970 --> 00:04:29,320
And while you're here,

39
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,530
I would like to introduce you to your editor.

40
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:34,290
And I want you to meet the people in the art department.

41
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:36,220
I'll set up an appointment with the marketing people.

42
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:38,580
When do you think we'll be through?

43
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,600
In about half an hour. Why?

44
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,600
I can't wait to tell Marilyn!
